+    # gen 86 (TNO_NS_LNR): local noise renormalisation of each night/group co-add before peak selection.  The cap
+    # fillers (z 4-6.5) are not static; they likely sit where the true noise exceeds what the weight map claims (star
+    # halos, edges, bad columns, sky residuals).  Per LNRT x LNRT tile, scale = 1.4826 * MAD(z) over covered pixels,
+    # divided by the median tile scale (only LOCAL excess counts), bilinearly upsampled, floored at 1.  Peaks are
+    # found/ranked on z / scale and the forced read-out map NMs is built from z / scale too (a fake pair in a noisy
+    # region must not get its 3-night support from that same noise).  ZK keeps raw z; ceiling test uses raw z.
+    LNR = os.environ.get("TNO_NS_LNR", "1") != "0"
+    LNRT = max(16, int(os.environ.get("TNO_NS_LNRT", "64"))); LNRMIN = int(os.environ.get("TNO_NS_LNRMIN", "512"))
